SR-RX recipe patch 0005 (+lab): no IERS / leap-second download.
Pinned SatDump 1aedd60 schedules IersDBHandler::updateIERS at every start (src-core/db/iers/iers_handler.cpp:33-52,
honor_setting is always true) and the task is due at once with an empty database (the decode unit's private HOME
is always empty): updateIERS fetches datacenter.iers.org and hpiers.obspm.fr over HTTPS (URLs fixed in the code,
not in satdump_cfg.json). The decode unit has no network (PrivateNetwork=yes, AF_UNIX only); this removes the
download itself. Only the AWS NAVATT reader reads the IERS table; the Meteor-M LRPT decode does not.
SatDump is GPL-3.0 (upstream LICENSE, git blob f288702d2fa16d3cdf0035b15a9fcbc552cd88e7). This change is distributed under the same licence.
---
diff --git a/src-core/db/iers/iers_handler.cpp b/src-core/db/iers/iers_handler.cpp
--- a/src-core/db/iers/iers_handler.cpp
+++ b/src-core/db/iers/iers_handler.cpp
@@ -54,6 +54,10 @@
 
     void IersDBHandler::updateIERS()
     {
+        // SR-RX +lab: no IERS / leap-second download. init() schedules this at every start and the task is
+        // due at once with an empty database; the two HTTPS URLs below are fixed in the code, not in the config.
+        return;
+
         std::string url_str = "https://datacenter.iers.org/products/eop/rapid/standard/json/finals2000A.all.json"; // TODOREWORK
 
         // IERS Bulletin A/B
